                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="490-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Violet Design Ltd. Flamingo Standard</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>Violet&#8217;s &#8220;Flamingo&#8221; line consists of four microphones:</p><ul><li>Flamingo Standard</li><li>Flamingo Vintage (described below)</li><li><a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Violet/Flamingo-ME">Flamingo ME</a></li><li>Flamingo Junior</li></ul><p>Here we&#8217;ll describe the Standard and Vintage models; follow the links above to read about the others. </p><p>The Flamingo Standard is a tube condenser with a fixed cardioid pickup pattern. The capsule is a dual-diaphragm 26mm design; the mylar membrane is sputtered with a proprietary gold alloy designed for &#8220;faster transient impulse response, minimum sound coloration, better low frequency response,&#8221; and higher SPL handling.</p><p>All Violet capsules are tested by hand in anechoic chambers prior to microphone assembly.</p><p>The Flamingo mics have multiple internal shockmounts, designed to individually isolate the capsule, head, electronics, and tube. In addition, the mic ships with an external shockmount.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s internal preamp is a Class &#8216;A,&#8217; discrete circuit and designed to provide clean output and an uncolored response. The vacuum tube is a 6267 and is mounted inside a heat sink.</p><p>A built-in humbucking transformer isolates the microphone from external interference and adds &#8220;analog warmth&#8221; to the sound.</p><p>The included power supply accommodates 100/120/220/240V environments and offers some unique features; it ramps up the voltage to the microphone slowly to protect the tube, and the microphone&#8217;s output (which like all tube mics is wired through the power supply) is muted until full voltage has been reached. An LED on the power supply case provides a voltage readout.</p><p>These mics ship in wooden boxes with a power supply (and cable), a shockmount, and printed manual.</p><p>The Standard Flamingo model is finished in violet.</p><p>The Flamingo Vintage differs from the Standard in only two respects:</p><ol><li>The capsule is tuned differently, to provide a warmer vocal sound with diminished highs (reminiscent of vintage tube mics), and </li><li>the body is painted matte black instead of purple.</li></ol><p><p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Violet/Flamingo-Standard">Violet Design Ltd. Flamingo Standard</a> is also known as: Flamingo.</p><p>The mic was released in 2007.</p>
